    "path": "charness-artifacts/release/2026-11-05-v8.16.0-notes.md",
    "prompt_content": "# Charness v8.16.0\n\nThis release ships the task-run lane work that had not been pushed before, led by the new Claude lane executor and its options, together with a fix to the debug planner.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The debug planner reads a `- Risk Class:` value apart from explanatory prose written after it, such as `none yet; ...`, `external-seam (...)` or `none -- ...`. Before this, the whole line was read as the value, so the prose counted as an unknown class. The planner then sent every new investigation in the repository to `repair-risk-declaration` and named another investigation's record as the file to repair. Now a valid value followed by prose is a valid declaration. A new subject starts its own record, and the earlier record stays with its subject. A line that opens with prose, or whose recognized classes include no forced class next to an unknown one, still routes to repair; a forced class next to an unknown one (`external-seam, bogus`) still interrupts, as before. `validate_debug_artifact.py` is unchanged and stays strict.\n- `charness task run --executor claude` runs a lane with `claude -p`. Sonnet is the default model, and `--claude-model haiku` selects Haiku. Codex stays the default executor. A Claude lane needs Linux bubblewrap. It runs inside a filesystem sandbox: the lane worktree, its private runtime and explicit `--grant-writable` directories are writable, and home configuration, credential files (including `~/.docker`) and shared Git configuration are not. Container daemon sockets (Docker, containerd, Podman, CRI-O) are masked, so a lane cannot drive the host's container daemon. The sandbox does not restrict network egress: a lane can reach any address the host can, including cloud metadata endpoints ([#889](https://github.com/corca-ai/charness/issues/889)). Provider credentials stay in a parent-side proxy. Commits go to private Git storage that the runner imports into the task branch afterwards, unless the caller grants the checkout's Git common directory, in which case the lane uses the shared linked-worktree Git directly. The result, report, branch, hooks, progress and verification contracts are the same as for other executors. `--grant-writable` now accepts Codex and Claude lanes and still refuses Muse. [docs/claude-task-executor.md](https://github.com/corca-ai/charness/blob/v8.16.0/docs/claude-task-executor.md) states the tested boundary and its limits. The real-sandbox tests ran on Linux with bubblewrap on the release machine; they skip where bubblewrap is absent, and CI does not install it.\n- The line that completes a command in a lane's events log now also carries `charness_duration_ms`. For a running lane, `task status <task-id> --commands` also reads the live stdout log, so it shows the current invocation's commands instead of nothing.\n- Lane environments: a lane's `TMPDIR`, `TMP` and `TEMP` are now the lane runtime root, so the npm, XDG, pip, ruff, pytest, coverage and pycache paths under it are writable inside a Muse sandbox. Before this, `npm pack` in a Muse lane failed with EROFS. Go's `GOCACHE`, `GOPATH` and `GOMODCACHE` now sit under the lane's cache home, which is private to the lane. A Codex or Claude caller can point it at a shared cache with `CHARNESS_TASK_RUN_CACHE_HOME`, but only inside a directory already granted with `--grant-writable`; the variable never adds a grant. A Codex lane no longer inherits `writable_roots` from the operator's configuration, so only its explicit runtime and `--add-dir` grants are writable, and read-only reviewers drop the lane-only overrides.\n- The lane progress rule records the lane's final output after the output capture drains, so the last window's progress counts. A failure of that last observation is ignored only when it is a recoverable I/O error.\n- When the Codex app-server exits before answering, the Codex host cache refresh in `charness update` now reports that it exited, instead of a response timeout.\n- Windows: runtime snapshots honour the Windows temporary-directory variables, scratch owner locking falls back to Windows byte-range locks where `flock` is missing, reviewer command lines use Windows argument quoting (spaces and quotes; `cmd.exe` metacharacters such as `&` and `%` are not escaped yet, [#890](https://github.com/corca-ai/charness/issues/890)), critique packet producers named `python3` run with the current Python interpreter, and the scratch inventory reports file sizes and repository paths consistently. Linux unit tests cover the argument quoting, interpreter selection and path normalisation; the byte-range lock fallback has no test, CI runs on Linux, and this release claims no run on a Windows host.\n- Release repairs to the test suite: these tests, whose verdict depended on machine load, now wait on the event they check. `test_codex_cache_refresh_accepts_real_initialize_shape_and_lifecycle_notifications` (and the other Codex app-server refresh tests) inject the reader's clock and wait for the fake's output instead of a `0.5` s deadline; `test_update_from_explicit_checkout_refreshes_surface` (with the other entry spawn tests) waits for the `charness` process to exit instead of a `28` s bound, and no longer launches a host `codex`; `test_worker_timeout_keeps_started_and_non_approval_state` runs the review wrapper in-process with only the worker's own deadline, so the outer runner bound cannot race it.\n\n## Update\n\nRun `charness update`, then run `charness version` to confirm the installed version. No migration is required. A launcher that relied on a Codex lane writing under a `writable_roots` path from the operator's own Codex configuration must now pass that directory with `--grant-writable`.\n\n## Derived claim surfaces\n\n<!-- charness:derived-claims:begin -->\n<!-- Generated from the shipped tree. Hand-edits are refused at publish: the gate re-derives this block and compares. -->\n\n<!-- claim-surface: json-declaring-scripts -->\n\n```yaml\nid: json-declaring-scripts\nquestion: which repo-owned Python sources declare their own `--json` option\ncount: 0\nitems: []\nscanned:\n- scripts/**/*.py\n- skills/**/scripts/**/*.py\n- charness\nunscanned:\n- the exported `plugins/charness/**` mirror and `mutants/**`, which are generated\n  copies of these same sources\n- flag names composed at runtime from a variable rather than written as a string literal\n- flags a wrapper forwards without declaring, which no parser in this tree names\n```\n\n<!-- claim-surface: charness-subcommands -->\n\n```yaml\nid: charness-subcommands\nquestion: which top-level subcommands the `charness` CLI declares\ncount: 14\nitems:\n- capability\n- catalog\n- doctor\n- goal\n- hooks\n- init\n- reset\n- task\n- tool\n- train\n- uninstall\n- update\n- version\n- worktree\nscanned:\n- charness\nunscanned:\n- nested subcommand groups such as `charness task run`, which are declared on their\n  own subparser\n- subcommands a host adapter adds outside this entrypoint\n```\n\n<!-- claim-surface: public-skills -->\n\n```yaml\nid: public-skills\nquestion: which public skills this repo ships\ncount: 19\nitems:\n- achieve\n- announcement\n- create-cli\n- create-skill\n- critique\n- debug\n- gather\n- hitl\n- hotl\n- ideation\n- impl\n- issue\n- narrative\n- prove\n- quality\n- release\n- retro\n- setup\n- spec\nscanned:\n- skills/public/*/SKILL.md\nunscanned:\n- support, profile, and integration skills, which are not part of the public surface\n- skills a consuming repo installs from elsewhere\n```\n\n<!-- claim-surface: repo-shell-gates -->\n\n```yaml\nid: repo-shell-gates\nquestion: which `check-*.sh` shell gates this repo ships\ncount: 8\nitems:\n- check-docs.sh\n- check-links-external.sh\n- check-links-internal.sh\n- check-markdown.sh\n- check-python-lint.sh\n- check-rust.sh\n- check-secrets.sh\n- check-shell.sh\nscanned:\n- scripts/**/check-*.sh\nunscanned:\n- Python gates under `scripts/`, which are far more numerous and are not this surface\n- gates a consuming repo wires from its own tree\n```\n\n<!-- charness:derived-claims:end -->\n",
    "prompt_encoding": "utf-8",
    "size_bytes": 7929,
    "source": "working-tree:charness-artifacts/release/2026-11-05-v8.16.0-notes.md"
  },
  {
    "carrier_path": "/home/hwidong/.cache/tmp/charness/runtime/811b9f8f8a808bfa/scratch/critique-review/review-b5bbc37c172e4ada2406fa851ae671fb/semantic-input/0002-content.bin",
    "carrier_sha256": "7d2636d2dffd3aedf051315f887c462ee6b32e78cb8c180b02d5eaf99ca3a3e0",
    "content_sha256": "d978463a17976db436df35265d5a49a6381e91e55726dbae296f8d3c100beb0a",
    "disposition": "present",
    "path": "docs/claude-task-executor.md",
    "prompt_content": "# Claude task executor\n\n> Status: current\n> Source of truth: [task_run_claude_sandbox.py](../scripts/task_run/task_run_claude_sandbox.py) and [task_run_claude_auth.py](../scripts/task_run/task_run_claude_auth.py)\n> Last verified: 2026-10-25\n\n`charness task run --executor claude --claude-model sonnet --effort medium`\nruns `claude -p` with the selected model. Sonnet is the lane default;\n`--claude-model haiku` selects `claude-haiku-5-5`. The Sonnet family uses the\nClaude CLI’s `sonnet` alias. The selected command model is recorded in\n`executor.model`; effort stays orchestration metadata.\nThe default executor remains Codex. The host currently requires Linux bubblewrap.\nClaude accepts validated `--grant-writable` host-state directories. Muse still refuses them.\n\nClaude lanes keep the same result/report, branch, hooks, progress and verification\ncontracts. Stream JSON remains in `claude.events.log`; terminal text becomes the\nreport, and steers resume the observed session. The process runs with the lane\nworktree as its current directory.\n\nThe Claude adapter wraps the entire process in a filesystem sandbox, supplies\nper-invocation permission settings, and isolates home/config/cache state under\nthe private execution runtime. The worktree, private runtime and explicit host-state grants are writable.\nPrivate Git storage allows normal commits and hooks without granting the agent\nwrites into the parent repository; the trusted runner imports the task branch\nafter execution. When the caller explicitly grants this checkout’s resolved Git\ncommon directory, the lane instead uses its native linked-worktree Git directory:\ncommits and hook attestations are immediately visible in shared Git, and no\nprivate import runs. Native Git discovers the existing linked `.git`; private mode\nmounts a protected private `gitdir:` pointer over that file only inside the sandbox.\nClaude receives no process-wide Git repository selectors, so foreign cwd and `-C`\nlookups retain their own repository identity. Private preparation and import select\nthe private repository for individual Git invocations only. Shared Git configuration remains read-only. Callers must\nexplicitly grant any external tool/verification caches their gates use.\nNative tools receive private writable `/tmp` for OS-level locks even when they ignore `TMPDIR`. Known temporary trees containing the worktree, runtime, Git object source and explicit grants retain read-only visibility before writable descendants are restored. Host temporary files remain unwritable. `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` is a private mode-0700 directory.\nReal home configuration and credential files remain protected, including\n`~/.docker`. Container daemon sockets (Docker, containerd, Podman, CRI-O) are\nmasked, because a read-only bind does not stop a connect.\nThe sandbox does not restrict network egress: a lane can reach any address the\nhost can, including cloud metadata endpoints and host TCP services\n([#889](https://github.com/corca-ai/charness/issues/889)).\nReal provider credentials stay in a parent-side proxy; the child receives an\ninvocation token. Credential-shaped workspace files are masked from shell reads\nas well as denied to file tools. The safety and real-lane evidence record states\nthe tested host boundary. The real-sandbox tests skip where bubblewrap is\nabsent, and CI does not install it.\n\nCredential masks cover known `.env*`, `.pem`, `.key` and credential filenames,\nnot arbitrary secret-bearing content. The API proxy forwards only to the fixed\nAnthropic HTTPS upstream and requires its per-invocation placeholder token.\n\nThe trusted importer reads a no-follow bundle byte copy, verifies its prerequisites\nand ancestry, and updates only the current task branch. Hooks stay enabled on\nlane commits inside the sandbox. Host metadata import disables hooks and fsmonitor\nso agent-edited hook files cannot escape the filesystem boundary during import.\n\nThe [task-run contract](./agent-task-runs.md) owns completion and retention.\n\nFor Claude lanes, the separate Codex preflight uses a private home under the\nretained execution runtime and inherits authentication only. It copies no real\nconfiguration or sessions. That reviewer-home subtree is masked from Claude,\nincluding shell reads, after the runtime receives its writable grant. Both\nprocess environments rebind Claude, Codex, Ceal and XDG state destinations to\ntheir private home even when the caller exports explicit session directories.\n",
    "prompt_encoding": "utf-8",
    "size_bytes": 4450,
    "source": "working-tree:docs/claude-task-executor.md"
  },
  {
    "carrier_path": "/home/hwidong/.cache/tmp/charness/runtime/811b9f8f8a808bfa/scratch/critique-review/review-b5bbc37c172e4ada2406fa851ae671fb/semantic-input/0003-content.bin",
    "carrier_sha256": "a7582f77fc4d3650e9fc9845f393205cb8e9b0b87fd4153f3c92b805f6e18803",
    "content_sha256": "a9c1214c08421e094a054f2ed6aa39bc05892b02a8ca1bc704adb9e9fd85f0bd",
    "disposition": "present",
    "path": "scripts/task_run/task_run_claude_sandbox.py",
    "prompt_content": "\"\"\"Claude lanes: OS write confinement, private home and private Git administration.\n\nThe complete Claude process (including hooks and file tools) runs behind bwrap;\nClaude's Bash-only sandbox cannot enforce this boundary. Runtime retention is\nowned by the enclosing task-run runtime. By default a trusted host imports the lane branch after execution. Explicitly\ngranting the checkout’s common Git directory selects native shared Git instead.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport stat\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Mapping, Sequence\n\n\ndef _load_repo_runtime_bootstrap():\n    pathlib, sys = __import__(\"pathlib\"), __import__(\"sys\")\n    marker = (\"scripts\", \"adapter_lib.py\")\n    parents = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents\n    root = next((p for p in parents if p.joinpath(*marker).is_file()), None)\n    if root is not None and str(root) not in sys.path:\n        sys.path.insert(0, str(root))\n\n\n_load_repo_runtime_bootstrap()\n\nfrom scripts.cli.bootstrap import managed_checkout_root  # noqa: E402\nfrom scripts.core.subprocess_guard import run_process  # noqa: E402\nfrom scripts.task_run.task_run_claude_auth import (  # noqa: E402\n    claude_auth_proxy as claude_auth_proxy,\n)\nfrom scripts.task_run.task_run_claude_review import reviewer_home  # noqa: E402\nfrom scripts.task_run.task_run_contract import TASK_CLAUDE_MODEL, TaskRunError  # noqa: E402\n\n_SECRET_DIRECTORIES = (\".claude\", \".codex\", \".ceal\", \".ssh\", \".aws\", \".azure\", \".kube\", \".docker\", \".gnupg\", \".config\", \".local/state/ceal\")\n# Container daemon sockets grant host-root-equivalent control to any member of\n# their group; a read-only root bind does not stop connect(). Mask each one.\n_HOST_DAEMON_SOCKETS = (\"/run/docker.sock\", \"/var/run/docker.sock\", \"/run/containerd/containerd.sock\",\n                        \"/run/podman/podman.sock\", \"/run/crio/crio.sock\")\n_SECRET_FILES = (\".claude.json\", \".netrc\", \".npmrc\", \".git-credentials\", \".bashrc\", \".bash_profile\", \".profile\", \".zshrc\", \".zshenv\", \".zprofile\")\n_GIT_ENV_KEYS = (\"GIT_DIR\", \"GIT_COMMON_DIR\", \"GIT_WORK_TREE\", \"GIT_INDEX_FILE\", \"GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY\", \"GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES\")\n\n\ndef _bounded_paths(worktree: Path, runtime: Path) -> tuple[Path, Path]:\n    worktree, runtime = worktree.resolve(), runtime.resolve()\n    home = Path.home().resolve()\n    if any(home.is_relative_to(path) for path in (worktree, runtime)):\n        raise TaskRunError(\"Claude worktree/runtime must not cover the operator home\")\n    if worktree.is_relative_to(runtime) or runtime.is_relative_to(worktree):\n        raise TaskRunError(\"Claude worktree/runtime roots must be separate bounded directories\")\n    return worktree, runtime\n\n\ndef _paths(runtime: Path) -> tuple[Path, Path, Path]:\n    root = runtime.resolve() / \"claude\"\n    return root, root / \"home\", root / \"git\"\n\n\ndef _git(worktree: Path, *args: str, git_dir: Path | None = None) -> str:\n    env = {key: value for key, value in os.environ.items()\n           if key not in _GIT_ENV_KEYS and not key.startswith(\"GIT_CONFIG_\")}\n    if git_dir is not None:\n        env.update(GIT_DIR=str(git_dir), GIT_WORK_TREE=str(worktree))\n    result = run_process([\"git\", \"-c\", \"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\", \"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\",\n                          \"-c\", \"protocol.ext.allow=never\", *args], cwd=worktree, env=env)\n    if result.returncode:\n        # Git output can contain hook/provider bodies. The operation name is enough.\n        raise TaskRunError(f\"Claude private Git operation failed: {args[0]}\")\n    return result.stdout.strip()\n\n\ndef _prepare_git(worktree: Path, runtime: Path) -> None:\n    root, _home, private = _paths(runtime)\n    marker = root / \"git-identity.json\"\n    if marker.exists():\n        identity = json.loads(marker.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n        if identity[\"worktree\"] != str(worktree):\n            raise TaskRunError(\"Claude runtime belongs to another worktree\")\n        return\n    branch = _git(worktree, \"symbolic-ref\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\")\n    base = _git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    common = Path(_git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-common-dir\"))\n    _git(worktree, \"init\", \"--bare\", str(private))\n    (private / \"objects/info/alternates\").write_text(str(common / \"objects\") + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    _git(worktree, \"config\", \"core.bare\", \"false\", git_dir=private)\n    _git(worktree, \"config\", \"core.worktree\", str(worktree), git_dir=private)\n    hook_result = run_process([\"git\", \"config\", \"--path\", \"core.hooksPath\"], cwd=worktree)\n    hooks = Path(hook_result.stdout.strip()) if hook_result.returncode == 0 else common / \"hooks\"\n    if not hooks.is_absolute():\n        hooks = worktree / hooks\n    _git(worktree, \"config\", \"core.hooksPath\", str(hooks.resolve()), git_dir=private)\n    # Resolve the trusted repository identity before isolating HOME. The agent\n    # cannot change this private configuration, and ambient author overrides\n    # are removed from its environment.\n    for setting in (\"user.name\", \"user.email\"):\n        _git(worktree, \"config\", setting, _git(worktree, \"config\", \"--get\", setting), git_dir=private)\n    _git(worktree, \"symbolic-ref\", \"HEAD\", f\"refs/heads/{branch}\", git_dir=private)\n    _git(worktree, \"update-ref\", f\"refs/heads/{branch}\", base, git_dir=private)\n    _git(worktree, \"read-tree\", \"HEAD\", git_dir=private)\n    # Preserve the lane's actual staged candidate on a same-worktree continuation.\n    index = Path(_git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-path\", \"index\"))\n    if index.is_file():\n        shutil.copyfile(index, private / \"index\")\n    marker.write_text(json.dumps({\"worktree\": str(worktree), \"branch\": branch, \"base\": base}), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef _sandbox_git(worktree: Path, runtime: Path, *args: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Never interpret the agent's private Git configuration on the host.\"\"\"\n    root, home, private = _paths(runtime)\n    env = {\"PATH\": os.defpath, \"HOME\": str(home), \"TMPDIR\": str(root / \"tmp\"),\n           \"GIT_DIR\": str(private), \"GIT_WORK_TREE\": str(worktree),\n           \"GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM\": \"1\", \"GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL\": \"/dev/null\"}\n    result = run_process([*sandbox_prefix(worktree, runtime), \"--\", \"git\", *args], cwd=worktree, env=env)\n    if result.returncode:\n        raise TaskRunError(f\"Claude sandboxed Git operation failed: {args[0]}\")\n    return result.stdout.strip()\n\n\ndef _copy_bundle_for_host(bundle: Path, runtime: Path) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"A no-follow byte copy crosses from untrusted runtime into host storage.\"\"\"\n    source_fd = os.open(bundle, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)\n    with os.fdopen(source_fd, \"rb\") as source:\n        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(source.fileno()).st_mode):\n            raise TaskRunError(\"Claude candidate bundle must be a regular file\")\n        with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(dir=runtime.parent, prefix=\"claude-import-\", delete=False) as target:\n            shutil.copyfileobj(source, target)\n            replacement = Path(target.name)\n    trusted = runtime.parent / \"claude-candidate.bundle\"\n    os.replace(replacement, trusted)\n    return trusted\n\n\ndef finalize_claude_git(worktree: Path, execution_runtime_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Import a verified bundle without running private Git config on the host.\n\n    The canonical host worktree owns the destination branch. Private queries and\n    bundle production stay sandboxed with no auth. Host index state is rebuilt\n    from the imported commit; any uncommitted work remains visible as dirty.\n    \"\"\"\n    worktree, runtime = _bounded_paths(worktree, execution_runtime_path)\n    root, _home, private = _paths(runtime)\n    marker = root / \"git-identity.json\"\n    if not marker.is_file():\n        return\n    identity = json.loads(marker.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    branch = _git(worktree, \"symbolic-ref\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\")\n    current = _git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    if identity != {\"worktree\": str(worktree), \"branch\": branch, \"base\": current}:\n        raise TaskRunError(\"Claude lane Git identity changed before import\")\n    ref = f\"refs/heads/{branch}\"\n    tip = _sandbox_git(worktree, runtime, \"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", ref)\n    if re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{40}(?:[0-9a-f]{24})?\", tip) is None:\n        raise TaskRunError(\"Claude private task branch has no valid commit\")\n    if _sandbox_git(worktree, runtime, \"symbolic-ref\", \"--short\", \"HEAD\") != branch:\n        raise TaskRunError(\"Claude changed the private task branch\")\n    if tip != current:\n        bundle = root / \"candidate.bundle\"\n        _sandbox_git(worktree, runtime, \"bundle\", \"create\", str(bundle), ref, f\"^{current}\")\n        trusted = _copy_bundle_for_host(bundle, runtime)\n        _git(worktree, \"bundle\", \"verify\", str(trusted))\n        _git(worktree, \"fetch\", \"--no-write-fetch-head\", \"--no-tags\", str(trusted), ref)\n        _git(worktree, \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", current, tip)\n        _git(worktree, \"update-ref\", ref, tip, current)\n    _git(worktree, \"read-tree\", \"HEAD\")\n    identity[\"base\"] = tip\n    marker.write_text(json.dumps(identity), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef _shared_git_dir(worktree: Path, writable_dirs: Sequence[Path]) -> Path | None:\n    \"\"\"Only an explicit grant of this checkout's common dir opts into native Git.\"\"\"\n    if not writable_dirs:\n        return None\n    common = Path(_git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-common-dir\")).resolve()\n    if common not in [Path(path).resolve() for path in writable_dirs]:\n        return None\n    return Path(_git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"--absolute-git-dir\"))\n\n\ndef configure_claude_environment(\n    env: dict[str, str], worktree: Path, execution_runtime_path: Path,\n    *, writable_dirs: Sequence[Path] = (),\n) -> dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Isolate home and auth without logging or copying the real credential store.\"\"\"\n    worktree, execution_runtime_path = _bounded_paths(worktree, execution_runtime_path)\n    root, home, private = _paths(execution_runtime_path)\n    for directory in (root, home, home / \".claude\", root / \"tmp\", root / \"cache\"):\n        directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (root / \"run\").mkdir(mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)\n    runtime_fd = os.open(root / \"run\", os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)\n    try:\n        os.fchmod(runtime_fd, 0o700)\n    finally:\n        os.close(runtime_fd)\n    configured = dict(env)\n    for name in list(configured):\n        if name in _GIT_ENV_KEYS or name.startswith((\"GIT_CONFIG_\", \"GIT_AUTHOR_\", \"GIT_COMMITTER_\")):\n            configured.pop(name, None)\n    # This native flag forces an additional Bash sandbox on Linux even when\n    # sandbox.enabled is false. Auth is isolated by our parent-side proxy.\n    for name in (\"CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB\", \"BASH_ENV\", \"ENV\", \"ZDOTDIR\", \"SSH_AUTH_SOCK\", \"GIT_SSH_COMMAND\", \"GIT_ASKPASS\",\n                 \"ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS\", \"CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK\", \"CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX\", \"CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY\"):\n        configured.pop(name, None)\n    configured.update(\n        HOME=str(home), CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=str(home / \".claude\"),\n        CODEX_HOME=str(home / \".codex\"), CEAL_HOME=str(home / \".ceal\"),\n        XDG_STATE_HOME=str(home / \".local/state\"),\n        CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR=str(root / \"tmp\"), TMPDIR=str(root / \"tmp\"),\n        TMP=str(root / \"tmp\"), TEMP=str(root / \"tmp\"),\n        XDG_CONFIG_HOME=str(home / \".config\"), XDG_CACHE_HOME=str(root / \"cache\"),\n        XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=str(root / \"run\"),\n        CHARNESS_CLAUDE_GIT_MODE=\"shared\" if _shared_git_dir(worktree, writable_dirs) else \"private\",\n        DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=\"1\",\n        GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=\"1\", GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=\"/dev/null\",\n    )\n    if not any(configured.get(name) for name in (\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\", \"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\", \"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\")):\n        credentials = Path.home() / \".claude/.credentials.json\"\n        try:\n            token = json.loads(credentials.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"claudeAiOauth\"][\"accessToken\"]\n        except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):\n            token = None\n        if token:\n            configured[\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\"] = token\n    return configured\n\n\ndef _settings(worktree: Path, runtime: Path, writable_dirs: Sequence[Path] = ()) -> Path:\n    root, _home, _private = _paths(runtime)\n    home = Path.home()\n    sensitive = [home / path for path in (*_SECRET_DIRECTORIES, *_SECRET_FILES)]\n    sensitive.append(reviewer_home(runtime))\n    deny = [f\"Read(/{path}/**)\" for path in sensitive]\n    deny += [f\"Read(/{path})\" for path in sensitive]\n    deny += [f\"Edit(/{path}/**)\" for path in sensitive]\n    deny += [f\"Edit(/{path})\" for path in sensitive]\n    deny += [\"Read(//proc/**)\", \"Read(**/.env)\", \"Read(**/.env.*)\", \"Read(**/*.pem)\", \"Read(**/*.key)\", \"Bash(git push *)\"]\n    grants = [permission for path in writable_dirs\n              for permission in (f\"Edit(/{path}/**)\", f\"Read(/{path}/**)\")]\n    settings = {\n        \"permissions\": {\n            \"defaultMode\": \"dontAsk\", \"disableBypassPermissionsMode\": \"disable\",\n            \"allow\": [*grants, \"Bash(*)\", f\"Edit(/{worktree}/**)\", f\"Read(/{worktree}/**)\", f\"Read(/{runtime.resolve()}/**)\", f\"Edit(/{runtime.resolve()}/**)\"],\n            \"deny\": deny,\n        },\n        # Outer bwrap covers the whole process, including hooks/file tools. The\n        # built-in Bash-only sandbox would need socat and widen git write access.\n        \"sandbox\": {\"enabled\": False, \"allowUnsandboxedCommands\": False},\n    }\n    settings_path = root / \"settings.json\"\n    settings_path.write_text(json.dumps(settings), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return settings_path\n\n\ndef _credential_files(worktree: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    \"\"\"Find known secret filenames in source, without traversing dependencies.\"\"\"\n    paths: set[Path] = set()\n    credential_names = {\"credentials\", \"credentials.json\", \".credentials.json\", \".netrc\", \".npmrc\", \"id_rsa\", \"id_ed25519\"}\n    for root, directories, files in os.walk(worktree, followlinks=False):\n        directories[:] = [name for name in directories if name not in\n                          {\".git\", \"node_modules\", \".cache\", \".venv\", \"venv\", \"__pycache__\"}]\n        for name in files:\n            if name.startswith(\".env\") or name.endswith((\".pem\", \".key\")) or name in credential_names:\n                path = Path(root) / name\n                if path.is_file():\n                    paths.add(path.resolve())\n    for path in Path.home().glob(\".env*\"):\n        if path.is_file():\n            paths.add(path.resolve())\n    return sorted(paths)\n\n\ndef sandbox_prefix(worktree: Path, execution_runtime_path: Path, *,  # noqa: C901 - one ordered bwrap argv; split tracked in #888\n                   writable_dirs: Sequence[Path] = ()) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return the OS boundary shared by Claude and the adversarial safety probe.\"\"\"\n    bwrap = shutil.which(\"bwrap\")\n    if bwrap is None:\n        raise TaskRunError(\"Claude executor requires bubblewrap for whole-process confinement\")\n    worktree, runtime = _bounded_paths(worktree, execution_runtime_path)\n    home = Path.home().resolve()\n    root, _home, private = _paths(runtime)\n    root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    mask = root / \"empty-credential\"\n    mask_fd = os.open(mask, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)\n    try:\n        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(mask_fd).st_mode):\n            raise TaskRunError(\"Claude credential mask must be a regular file\")\n        os.ftruncate(mask_fd, 0)\n    finally:\n        os.close(mask_fd)\n    command = [bwrap, \"--die-with-parent\", \"--new-session\", \"--unshare-pid\", \"--unshare-ipc\", \"--unshare-uts\", \"--ro-bind\", \"/\", \"/\", \"--proc\", \"/proc\", \"--dev\", \"/dev\"]\n    # Native tools can use OS /tmp rather than TMPDIR for locks. Give them\n    # private scratch storage; never grant writes to the host temporary root.\n    # Later binds restore the worktree, runtime and explicit caches under /tmp.\n    command.extend((\"--tmpfs\", \"/tmp\"))\n    # Preserve read access to known temporary trees (including private Git's\n    # object source), then restore only their explicitly writable descendants.\n    read_paths = [worktree, runtime, *writable_dirs]\n    if (worktree / \".git\").exists():\n        read_paths.append(Path(_git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-common-dir\")).resolve())\n    temporary_root = Path(\"/tmp\")\n    read_roots = {temporary_root / path.relative_to(temporary_root).parts[0]\n                  for path in read_paths if path.is_relative_to(temporary_root) and path != temporary_root}\n    for path in sorted(read_roots):\n        command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(path), str(path)))\n    # Explicit grants precede all secret and policy masks.\n    for path in writable_dirs:\n        command.extend((\"--bind\", str(path), str(path)))\n    for name in _SECRET_DIRECTORIES:\n        path = home / name\n        if path.exists():\n            command.extend((\"--tmpfs\", str(path), \"--remount-ro\", str(path)))\n    for name in _SECRET_FILES:\n        path = home / name\n        if path.exists():\n            command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(mask), str(path)))\n    # A process must not reach host Unix sockets (SSH agents, daemon APIs).\n    for path in (Path(\"/run/user\") / str(os.getuid()),):\n        if path.exists():\n            command.extend((\"--tmpfs\", str(path), \"--remount-ro\", str(path)))\n    for path in sorted({Path(socket).resolve() for socket in _HOST_DAEMON_SOCKETS if Path(socket).exists()}):\n        command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(mask), str(path)))\n    command.extend((\"--bind\", str(worktree), str(worktree), \"--bind\", str(runtime), str(runtime)))\n    # Policy and Git identity remain protected through the writable grants.\n    # Shared Git is read-only unless the caller explicitly grants it.\n    root, _home, private = _paths(runtime)\n    # Make each policy-bearing ancestor a mountpoint too. A file-only mount\n    # otherwise permits renaming its ancestor and recreating a writable policy.\n    for directory in (root, private):\n        if directory.exists():\n            command.extend((\"--bind\", str(directory), str(directory)))\n    command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(mask), str(mask)))\n    for path in (worktree / \".git\", root / \"git-identity.json\", root / \"settings.json\", private / \"config\"):\n        if path.exists():\n            command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(path), str(path)))\n    shared_git = _shared_git_dir(worktree, writable_dirs)\n    if shared_git is None and private.exists() and (worktree / \".git\").is_file():\n        # Scope private discovery to this worktree's mount namespace. Exported\n        # selectors would override every foreign cwd/-C lookup in child tools.\n        pointer = root / \"git-discovery\"\n        pointer.write_text(f\"gitdir: {private}\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(pointer), str(pointer),\n                        \"--ro-bind\", str(pointer), str(worktree / \".git\")))\n    if shared_git is not None:\n        common = Path(_git(worktree, \"rev-parse\", \"--path-format=absolute\", \"--git-common-dir\"))\n        # Mount each linked-admin ancestor so renaming it cannot replace policy.\n        for directory in reversed((shared_git, *shared_git.parents)):\n            if directory != common and directory.is_relative_to(common):\n                command.extend((\"--bind\", str(directory), str(directory)))\n        for path in (common / \"config\", common / \"config.worktree\", shared_git / \"config.worktree\"):\n            if path.exists():\n                command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(path), str(path)))\n    private_review = reviewer_home(runtime)\n    if private_review.exists():\n        command.extend((\"--tmpfs\", str(private_review), \"--remount-ro\", str(private_review)))\n    for path in _credential_files(worktree):\n        command.extend((\"--ro-bind\", str(mask), str(path)))\n    command.extend((\"--chdir\", str(worktree)))\n    return command\n\n\ndef build_claude_command(\n    executable: str, worktree: Path, execution_runtime_path: Path, *, model: str = TASK_CLAUDE_MODEL,\n    writable_dirs: Sequence[Path] = (),\n) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Prepare a resumable isolated lane; stdin supplies its prompt.\"\"\"\n    worktree, runtime = _bounded_paths(worktree, execution_runtime_path)\n    configure_claude_environment({}, worktree, runtime, writable_dirs=writable_dirs)\n    if _shared_git_dir(worktree, writable_dirs) is None:\n        _prepare_git(worktree, runtime)\n    settings = _settings(worktree, runtime, writable_dirs)\n    # Load only the managed plugin; private HOME must not import operator settings.\n    plugin = managed_checkout_root(Path.home()) / \"plugins\" / \"charness\"\n    return [*sandbox_prefix(worktree, runtime, writable_dirs=writable_dirs), \"--\", executable, \"-p\", \"--model\", model,\n            \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--verbose\", \"--permission-mode\", \"dontAsk\",\n            \"--permission-prompts\", \"none\", \"--settings\", str(settings), \"--setting-sources\", \"project\",\n            \"--plugin-dir\", str(plugin), \"--strict-mcp-config\", \"--mcp-config\", '{\"mcpServers\":{}}']\n\n\ndef finalize_executor_candidate(\n    result: dict[str, Any], executor: str, worktree: Path, env: Mapping[str, str],\n) -> None:\n    if executor != \"claude\":\n        return\n\n    runtime = Path(env[\"CHARNESS_RUNTIME_ROOT\"])\n    if env.get(\"CHARNESS_CLAUDE_GIT_MODE\") == \"shared\":\n        return\n    try:\n        finalize_claude_git(worktree, runtime)\n    except (OSError, TaskRunError):\n        result[\"exec_error\"] = \"Claude private Git import failed; inspect retained runtime\"\n        result[\"exit_code\"] = 1\n",
    "prompt_encoding": "utf-8",
    "size_bytes": 21455,
    "source": "working-tree:scripts/task_run/task_run_claude_sandbox.py"
  },
  {
    "carrier_path": "/home/hwidong/.cache/tmp/charness/runtime/811b9f8f8a808bfa/scratch/critique-review/review-b5bbc37c172e4ada2406fa851ae671fb/semantic-input/0004-content.bin",
    "carrier_sha256": "f3684ca2d8a0737241c4d56454748e8c9826dc483c74e37b962b33a8239f9954",
    "content_sha256": "885bb6cd67a5d8fb2b9eca0d8f3fd0f58528ee5b3be86822c0d1bb4116440772",
    "disposition": "present",
    "path": "tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_claude_sandbox.py",
    "prompt_content": "\"\"\"Whole-process Claude boundary, private Git commits and home isolation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shlex\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom scripts.core.subprocess_guard import run_process\nfrom scripts.task_run import task_run_claude_sandbox as sandbox\n\n\ndef _git(root: Path, *args: str, env: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> str:\n    result = run_process([\"git\", *args], cwd=root, env=env)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, args[0]\n    return result.stdout.strip()\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"The actual OS sandbox must reject arbitrary-process outside writes\")\ndef test_arbitrary_process_write_outside_lane_is_refused(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\"):\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap not installed\")\n    lane = tmp_path / \"lane\"\n    runtime = tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    lane.mkdir()\n    runtime.mkdir()\n    outside = tmp_path / \"outside.txt\"\n    outside.write_text(\"unchanged\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    script = (\n        \"from pathlib import Path; import errno\\n\"\n        \"Path('inside.txt').write_text('allowed')\\n\"\n        f\"outside = Path({str(outside)!r})\\n\"\n        \"try:\\n outside.write_text('forbidden')\\n\"\n        \"except OSError as exc:\\n assert exc.errno in (errno.EROFS, errno.EACCES, errno.EPERM)\\n\"\n        \"else:\\n raise AssertionError('outside write escaped confinement')\\n\"\n        \"print('inside-write=allowed outside-write=refused')\\n\"\n    )\n    result = run_process([*sandbox.sandbox_prefix(lane, runtime), \"--\", sys.executable, \"-c\", script], cwd=lane)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    assert result.stdout.strip() == \"inside-write=allowed outside-write=refused\"\n    assert outside.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"unchanged\"\n    assert (lane / \"inside.txt\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"allowed\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"Private Git must retain hooks and import the task-branch commit back through the real reader\")\ndef test_private_git_commit_roundtrip_keeps_hooks_and_shared_git_readonly(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\"):\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap not installed\")\n    repo = tmp_path / \"repo\"\n    lane = tmp_path / \"lane\"\n    runtime = tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    repo.mkdir()\n    _git(repo, \"init\", \"--initial-branch=main\")\n    _git(repo, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"Test\")\n    _git(repo, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"test@example.com\")\n    (repo / \"doc.md\").write_text(\"typoo\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    _git(repo, \"add\", \"doc.md\")\n    _git(repo, \"commit\", \"-m\", \"seed\")\n    _git(repo, \"worktree\", \"add\", \"-b\", \"pilot\", str(lane))\n    _git(repo, \"config\", \"core.hooksPath\", \".hooks\")\n    (lane / \".hooks\").mkdir()\n    hook = lane / \".hooks/pre-commit\"\n    hook.write_text(\"#!/bin/sh\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' hook-ran > hook-proof\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    hook.chmod(0o755)\n    base = _git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    sandbox.build_claude_command(\"claude\", lane, runtime)\n    env = sandbox.configure_claude_environment(dict(os.environ), lane, runtime)\n    outside = tmp_path / \"outside-hook-proof\"\n    malicious_hook = \"#!/bin/sh\\n\" + \"printf escaped > \" + shlex.quote(str(outside)) + \"\\n\"\n    script = \"printf '%s\\\\n' typo > doc.md && git add doc.md && git commit -m typo\"\n    script += \" && printf %s \" + shlex.quote(malicious_hook) + \" > .hooks/reference-transaction && chmod +x .hooks/reference-transaction\"\n    result = run_process([*sandbox.sandbox_prefix(lane, runtime), \"--\", \"/bin/sh\", \"-c\", script], cwd=lane, env=env)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    assert (lane / \"hook-proof\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"hook-ran\\n\"\n    assert _git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\") == base\n    sandbox.finalize_claude_git(lane, runtime)\n    assert not outside.exists(), \"trusted metadata import ran a task-controlled hook\"\n    assert _git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\") != base\n    assert _git(lane, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"HEAD\") == \"\"\n    assert _git(lane, \"log\", \"-1\", \"--format=%an <%ae>\") == \"Test <test@example.com>\"\n    assert _git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"main\") == base\n    sandbox.finalize_claude_git(lane, runtime)\n\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"Claude Git discovery must honor foreign repositories while task commits roundtrip through private Git or explicit native grants\")\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"shared\", [False, True], ids=[\"private\", \"native\"])\ndef test_lane_git_discovery_respects_foreign_checkout(tmp_path: Path, shared: bool) -> None:\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\"):\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap not installed\")\n    repo, lane, foreign, runtime = [tmp_path / name for name in (\"repo\", \"lane\", \"foreign\", \"runtime\")]\n    for root in (repo, foreign):\n        root.mkdir()\n        _git(root, \"init\", \"--initial-branch=main\")\n        _git(root, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"Test\")\n        _git(root, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"test@example.com\")\n        _git(root, \"commit\", \"--allow-empty\", \"-m\", root.name)\n    base = _git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    foreign_head = _git(foreign, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    assert foreign_head != base\n    _git(repo, \"worktree\", \"add\", \"-b\", \"pilot\", str(lane))\n    writable = [repo / \".git\"] if shared else []\n    command = sandbox.build_claude_command(\"claude\", lane, runtime, writable_dirs=writable)\n    env = sandbox.configure_claude_environment(dict(os.environ, CHARNESS_RUNTIME_ROOT=str(runtime)),\n                                                lane, runtime, writable_dirs=writable)\n    prefix = command[:command.index(\"--\")]\n    code = (\n        \"import subprocess; from pathlib import Path\\n\"\n        \"def git(*args, cwd=None):\\n\"\n        \" return subprocess.check_output(['git',*args],cwd=cwd,text=True).strip()\\n\"\n        f\"assert git('-C',{str(foreign)!r},'rev-parse','HEAD') == {foreign_head!r}, 'foreign -C discovery'\\n\"\n        f\"assert git('rev-parse','HEAD',cwd={str(foreign)!r}) == {foreign_head!r}, 'foreign cwd discovery'\\n\"\n        \"Path('nested').mkdir()\\n\"\n        f\"assert git('rev-parse','HEAD',cwd='nested') == {base!r}\\n\"\n        \"git('commit','--allow-empty','-m','lane discovery')\\n\"\n        \"print(git('rev-parse','HEAD'))\\n\"\n    )\n    result = run_process([*prefix, \"--\", sys.executable, \"-c\", code], cwd=lane, env=env)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    tip = result.stdout.splitlines()[-1]\n    assert tip != base\n    assert _git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\") == (tip if shared else base)\n    finalized = {\"exit_code\": 0}\n    sandbox.finalize_executor_candidate(finalized, \"claude\", lane, env)\n    assert finalized == {\"exit_code\": 0}\n    assert _git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\") == tip\n    assert _git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"main\") == base\n    assert _git(foreign, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\") == foreign_head\n\n\n\ndef test_lane_loads_only_managed_charness_plugin(tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch) -> None:\n    from scripts.cli.bootstrap import managed_checkout_root\n\n    operator = tmp_path / \"operator\"\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox.Path, \"home\", lambda: operator)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox, \"_prepare_git\", lambda *_args: None)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox, \"sandbox_prefix\", lambda *_args, **_kwargs: [\"bwrap\"])\n    lane, runtime = tmp_path / \"lane\", tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    command = sandbox.build_claude_command(\"claude\", lane, runtime)\n    plugin = managed_checkout_root(operator) / \"plugins\" / \"charness\"\n    assert command.count(\"--plugin-dir\") == 1\n    assert command[command.index(\"--plugin-dir\") + 1] == str(plugin)\n    assert command[command.index(\"--setting-sources\") + 1] == \"project\"\n    assert \"--strict-mcp-config\" in command\n    assert command[command.index(\"--mcp-config\") + 1] == '{\"mcpServers\":{}}'\n    env = sandbox.configure_claude_environment({}, lane, runtime)\n    assert Path(env[\"HOME\"]).is_relative_to(runtime)\n    assert Path(env[\"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\"]).is_relative_to(runtime)\n\n\ndef test_claude_settings_and_environment_are_invocation_local(tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch) -> None:\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox.Path, \"home\", lambda: tmp_path / \"operator\")\n    lane, runtime = tmp_path / \"lane\", tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    runtime.mkdir()\n    (runtime / \"claude\").mkdir()\n    settings = json.loads(sandbox._settings(lane, runtime).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    env = sandbox.configure_claude_environment({\"BASH_ENV\": \"do-not-source\", \"GIT_DIR\": \"old\", \"CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB\": \"1\"}, lane, runtime)\n    assert \"BASH_ENV\" not in env\n    assert Path(env[\"HOME\"]).is_relative_to(runtime)\n    assert Path(env[\"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\"]).is_relative_to(runtime)\n    assert not any(key in env for key in (\"GIT_DIR\", \"GIT_WORK_TREE\", \"GIT_COMMON_DIR\"))\n    assert \"CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB\" not in env\n    assert settings[\"permissions\"][\"disableBypassPermissionsMode\"] == \"disable\"\n    assert \"Read(//proc/**)\" in settings[\"permissions\"][\"deny\"]\n    assert \"blockReadsOutsideWorkingDirectories\" not in settings[\"permissions\"]\n    assert \"Bash(*)\" in settings[\"permissions\"][\"allow\"]\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"which\", [\"home\", \"ancestor\", \"overlap\"])\ndef test_unbounded_sandbox_roots_are_refused(tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch, which: str) -> None:\n    operator_home = tmp_path / \"operator\"\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox.Path, \"home\", lambda: operator_home)\n    lane, runtime = tmp_path / \"lane\", tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    if which == \"home\":\n        runtime = operator_home\n    elif which == \"ancestor\":\n        runtime = tmp_path\n    else:\n        runtime = lane / \"runtime\"\n    with pytest.raises(sandbox.TaskRunError):\n        sandbox.configure_claude_environment({}, lane, runtime)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"Real loopback requests prove placeholder auth and fixed-upstream credential substitution\")\ndef test_auth_proxy_hides_credentials_and_authenticates_invocation(monkeypatch) -> None:\n    import http.client\n\n    from scripts.task_run import task_run_claude_auth as auth\n\n    captured = []\n\n    class Response:\n        status = 200\n\n        def getheaders(self):\n            return [(\"Content-Length\", \"2\"), (\"Authorization\", \"must-not-leave-proxy\")]\n\n        def read1(self, _size):\n            if captured[-1].get(\"read\"):\n                return b\"\"\n            captured[-1][\"read\"] = True\n            return b\"ok\"\n\n    class Upstream:\n        def __init__(self, host, timeout):\n            assert host == \"api.anthropic.com\"\n\n        def request(self, method, path, body, headers):\n            captured.append({\"method\": method, \"path\": path, \"body\": body, \"headers\": headers})\n\n        def getresponse(self):\n            return Response()\n\n        def close(self):\n            pass\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(auth.http.client, \"HTTPSConnection\", Upstream)\n    env = {\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\": \"test-upstream-credential\", \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\": \"unused-test-key\"}\n    with auth.claude_auth_proxy(env) as child:\n        assert child[\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\"] != env[\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\"]\n        assert \"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\" not in child\n        assert all(\"test-upstream-credential\" not in value for value in child.values())\n        address = child[\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\"].removeprefix(\"http://\")\n        connection = http.client.HTTPConnection(address)\n        connection.request(\"POST\", \"/v1/messages\", body=b\"{}\")\n        denied = connection.getresponse()\n        assert denied.status == 403\n        denied.read()\n        connection.close()\n        assert captured == []\n        connection = http.client.HTTPConnection(address)\n        connection.request(\"POST\", \"/v1/messages\", body=b\"{}\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + child[\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\"]})\n        response = connection.getresponse()\n        assert response.status == 200\n        assert response.getheader(\"Authorization\") is None\n        assert response.read() == b\"ok\"\n        connection.close()\n    assert captured[0][\"headers\"][\"Authorization\"] == \"Bearer test-upstream-credential\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"The real OS mount tree must prevent ancestor-rename policy replacement\")\ndef test_sandbox_policy_ancestors_cannot_be_replaced(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\"):\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap not installed\")\n    lane, runtime = tmp_path / \"lane\", tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    lane.mkdir()\n    private = runtime / \"claude/git\"\n    private.mkdir(parents=True)\n    policy = private / \"config\"\n    policy.write_text(\"protected\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    code = (\n        \"from pathlib import Path; import errno\\n\"\n        f\"paths = [Path({str(runtime / 'claude')!r}), Path({str(private)!r})]\\n\"\n        \"for path in paths:\\n\"\n        \" try:\\n  path.rename(path.with_name(path.name + '.old'))\\n\"\n        \" except OSError as exc:\\n  assert exc.errno in (errno.EBUSY, errno.EROFS, errno.EPERM)\\n\"\n        \" else:\\n  raise AssertionError('policy ancestor replacement escaped')\\n\"\n    )\n    result = run_process([*sandbox.sandbox_prefix(lane, runtime), \"--\", sys.executable, \"-c\", code], cwd=lane)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    assert policy.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"protected\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"Arbitrary Bash reads must not bypass credential-file permission rules\")\ndef test_preexisting_worktree_credentials_are_masked_for_subprocesses(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\"):\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap not installed\")\n    lane, runtime = tmp_path / \"lane\", tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    lane.mkdir()\n    runtime.mkdir()\n    secret = lane / \".env\"\n    secret.write_text(\"synthetic-credential-sentinel\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    code = (\"from pathlib import Path\\n\"\n            \"try:\\n value = Path('.env').read_text()\\n\"\n            \"except PermissionError:\\n pass\\n\"\n            \"else:\\n assert value == ''\\n\")\n    result = run_process([*sandbox.sandbox_prefix(lane, runtime), \"--\", sys.executable, \"-c\", code], cwd=lane)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    assert secret.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"synthetic-credential-sentinel\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"Explicit host grants must roundtrip native task-branch commits and gate receipts through the actual OS sandbox\")\ndef test_explicit_grants_allow_shared_git_and_gate_cache(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\"):\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap not installed\")\n    from scripts.task_run import task_run_lane_options as options, task_run_lane_runner as runner\n    from scripts.task_run.task_run_runtime import scrubbed_lane_env\n\n    repo, lane, runtime, cache = [tmp_path / name for name in (\"repo\", \"lane\", \"runtime\", \"cache\")]\n    repo.mkdir()\n    cache.mkdir()\n    _git(repo, \"init\", \"--initial-branch=main\")\n    _git(repo, \"config\", \"user.name\", \"Test\")\n    _git(repo, \"config\", \"user.email\", \"test@example.com\")\n    _git(repo, \"commit\", \"--allow-empty\", \"-m\", \"seed\")\n    _git(repo, \"worktree\", \"add\", \"-b\", \"pilot\", str(lane))\n    # A retained private runtime must not import its stale branch after opt-in.\n    sandbox.build_claude_command(\"claude\", lane, runtime)\n    common = repo / \".git\"\n    _git(repo, \"config\", \"extensions.worktreeConfig\", \"true\")\n    _git(lane, \"config\", \"--worktree\", \"user.name\", \"Test\")\n    linked = Path(_git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"--absolute-git-dir\"))\n    grants = options.resolve_granted_writable(repo, [common, cache], executor=\"claude\")\n    payload = {\"worktree_path\": str(lane)}\n    resolved = {\"git_common_dir\": common, \"granted_writable_dirs\": grants}\n    writable = runner.lane_writable_dirs(payload, resolved, common / \"worktrees/lane\", runtime,\n                                         executor=\"claude\", worktree=lane)\n    command = runner.lane_command(executor=\"claude\", executable=\"claude\", effort=\"medium\",\n                                  prompt=\"probe\", execution_runtime_path=runtime,\n                                  writable_dirs=writable, worktree=lane)\n    env = scrubbed_lane_env(payload, dict(os.environ, CHARNESS_RUNTIME_ROOT=str(runtime)), \"claude\")\n    base = _git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"main\")\n    receipt = common / \"ceal/pre-push-attestations/probe.jsonl\"\n    code = (\"from pathlib import Path; import subprocess\\n\"\n            f\"receipt=Path({str(receipt)!r}); receipt.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True); receipt.write_text('gate-pass\\\\n')\\n\"\n            f\"Path({str(cache / 'verification.json')!r}).write_text('verified')\\n\"\n            \"subprocess.run(['git','commit','--allow-empty','-m','sandbox probe'],check=True)\\n\"\n            f\"assert Path({str(common / 'config')!r}).read_text()\\n\"\n            f\"outside=Path({str(tmp_path / 'outside')!r})\\n\"\n            f\"config=Path({str(common / 'config')!r})\\n\"\n            \"try: config.write_text('changed')\\n\"\n            \"except OSError: pass\\n\"\n            \"else: raise AssertionError('shared Git policy writable')\\n\"\n            f\"linked=Path({str(linked)!r})\\n\"\n            \"try: (linked / 'config.worktree').write_text('changed')\\n\"\n            \"except OSError: pass\\n\"\n            \"else: raise AssertionError('linked Git policy writable')\\n\"\n            \"try: linked.rename(linked.with_name('replaced'))\\n\"\n            \"except OSError: pass\\n\"\n            \"else: raise AssertionError('linked policy ancestor replaceable')\\n\"\n            \"try: outside.write_text('escape')\\n\"\n            \"except OSError: pass\\n\"\n            \"else: raise AssertionError('outside grant writable')\\n\")\n    prefix = command[:command.index(\"--\")]\n    result = run_process([*prefix, \"--\", sys.executable, \"-c\", code], cwd=lane, env=env)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    assert payload[\"granted_writable_dirs\"] == grants\n    assert receipt.read_text() == \"gate-pass\\n\"\n    assert (cache / \"verification.json\").read_text() == \"verified\"\n    tip = _git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\")\n    assert tip != base\n    finalized = {\"exit_code\": 0}\n    sandbox.finalize_executor_candidate(finalized, \"claude\", lane, env)\n    assert finalized == {\"exit_code\": 0}\n    assert _git(lane, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\") == tip\n    assert _git(repo, \"rev-parse\", \"main\") == base\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"Native package managers must acquire private OS tmp locks without a writable host tmp grant\")\ndef test_private_tmp_allows_package_manager_locks_without_host_writes(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\"):\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap not installed\")\n    lane, runtime = tmp_path / \"lane\", tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    lane.mkdir()\n    runtime.mkdir()\n    env = sandbox.configure_claude_environment({}, lane, runtime)\n    lock_name = \"claude-package-manager-lock-\" + tmp_path.name\n    code = (\n        \"from pathlib import Path; import os\\n\"\n        f\"lock = Path('/tmp') / {lock_name!r}\\n\"\n        \"lock.mkdir(); (lock / 'lock').write_text('locked')\\n\"\n        \"assert (lock / 'lock').read_text() == 'locked'\\n\"\n        \"runtime = Path(os.environ['XDG_RUNTIME_DIR'])\\n\"\n        \"(runtime / 'runtime-lock').write_text('locked')\\n\"\n        \"assert runtime.stat().st_mode & 0o777 == 0o700\\n\"\n        \"print('package-manager-lock=write/read private-tmp=ok')\\n\"\n    )\n    result = run_process([*sandbox.sandbox_prefix(lane, runtime), \"--\", sys.executable, \"-c\", code], cwd=lane, env=env)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    assert result.stdout.strip() == \"package-manager-lock=write/read private-tmp=ok\"\n    assert not (Path('/tmp') / lock_name).exists()\n\n\ndef test_runtime_directory_reclaims_mode_without_following_symlinks(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    lane, runtime = tmp_path / \"lane\", tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    lane.mkdir()\n    runtime.mkdir()\n    sandbox.configure_claude_environment({}, lane, runtime)\n    run = runtime / \"claude/run\"\n    run.chmod(0o777)\n    sandbox.configure_claude_environment({}, lane, runtime)\n    assert run.stat().st_mode & 0o777 == 0o700\n    run.rename(run.with_name(\"previous-run\"))\n    outside = tmp_path / \"outside\"\n    outside.mkdir(mode=0o755)\n    before = outside.stat().st_mode\n    run.symlink_to(outside, target_is_directory=True)\n    with pytest.raises(OSError):\n        sandbox.configure_claude_environment({}, lane, runtime)\n    assert outside.stat().st_mode == before\n\n\ndef test_sandbox_masks_docker_credentials_and_host_daemon_sockets(monkeypatch, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"A docker-group member must not reach the daemon or registry auth from a lane.\"\"\"\n    home = tmp_path / \"home\"\n    (home / \".docker\").mkdir(parents=True)\n    lane = tmp_path / \"lane\"\n    runtime = tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    lane.mkdir()\n    runtime.mkdir()\n    daemon = tmp_path / \"daemon.sock\"  # existence is what the mask keys on\n    daemon.write_text(\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox.Path, \"home\", classmethod(lambda _cls: home))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox.shutil, \"which\", lambda _name: \"/usr/bin/bwrap\")\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sandbox, \"_HOST_DAEMON_SOCKETS\", (str(daemon), str(tmp_path / \"absent.sock\")))\n\n    command = sandbox.sandbox_prefix(lane, runtime)\n\n    mask = str(runtime.resolve() / \"claude\" / \"empty-credential\")\n    docker = str(home / \".docker\")\n    assert [\"--tmpfs\", docker, \"--remount-ro\", docker] in [command[i:i + 4] for i in range(len(command))]\n    assert [\"--ro-bind\", mask, str(daemon.resolve())] in [command[i:i + 3] for i in range(len(command))]\n    assert str(tmp_path / \"absent.sock\") not in command\n\n\n@pytest.mark.boundary_contract(reason=\"The real OS sandbox must refuse a connect to the host Docker daemon socket\")\ndef test_lane_cannot_connect_to_the_host_docker_socket(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    socket_path = Path(\"/run/docker.sock\")\n    if not shutil.which(\"bwrap\") or not socket_path.exists():\n        pytest.skip(\"bubblewrap or a host Docker socket is not present\")\n    lane = tmp_path / \"lane\"\n    runtime = tmp_path / \"runtime\"\n    lane.mkdir()\n    runtime.mkdir()\n    script = (\n        \"import socket\\n\"\n        \"s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX)\\n\"\n        \"try:\\n s.connect('/run/docker.sock')\\n\"\n        \"except OSError as exc:\\n print('refused', type(exc).__name__)\\n\"\n        \"else:\\n print('connected')\\n\"\n    )\n    result = run_process([*sandbox.sandbox_prefix(lane, runtime), \"--\", sys.executable, \"-c\", script], cwd=lane)\n    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr\n    assert result.stdout.startswith(\"refused\"), result.stdout\n",
